This seems convoluted...

The docker build command reads a Dockerfile and builds a Docker image based on the instructions in the file.

Grok has a massive explanation if I ever care to go through it.....

example:

```bash
cd dockerthings/
 
mkdir ash

cd ash

cp -r /var/www/html/ash/* .

ll #verify copy happened

cat > Dockerfile << EOL
FROM nginx:latest
COPY . /usr/share/nginx/html/
EOL

docker build -t ash .

docker images

docker run -d --name potato -p 8111:80 ash:latest
```